# Run_Structure_Design — Skeleton

## 1. Applies when
Roguelite / run-based games (roguelite).

## 2. This document owns
- Run anatomy: phases (start/mid/boss), length targets, biome/stage ordering rules.
- In-run progression: temporary upgrades, stacking rules, run-end wipe semantics.
- Death/exit handling and run summary design.

## 3. This document does NOT own
- Persistent unlocks — Meta_Progression_Design.
- Room/level generation — Level_Generation_Design.
- Enemy roster — Enemy_Design.

## 4. Recommended chapter structure
1. Run philosophy / 2. Anatomy & phases / 3. Stage ordering / 4. In-run upgrades / 5. Wipe semantics / 6. Death & summary / 7. Difficulty scaling / 8. Open questions

## 5. Common boundaries
- Run vs Meta: anything wiped on death is run-scope; anything kept is meta-scope — no dual-ownership stats.
- Run_Structure defines *shape*; Level_Generation fills it.

## 6. Common audit rules
- Every in-run upgrade declares its wipe class explicitly.
- Phase list matches the generation system's phase inputs.
